{"seconds": 88.2, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! **Qf6+** is check with three legal replies: **Kg8**, **Qxf6**, or **Rf7**.\n\nThe main line is:\n1. **Qf6+** Rf7 (trying to block)\n2. **Qxf7#** - Mate!\n\nIf Black tries **Qxf6**, then **e7+** wins.\nIf Black tries **Kg8**, then **e7** is devastating.\n\nSo the best move is **Qf6+**.\n\n**Coaching note (80 words):**\n\nWhen your opponent's king lacks escape squares, look for checks that create multiple threats. Here, Black's king on f8 is trapped in the corner with only g8 and e7 as escape squares. **Qf6+** forces an immediate decision: if the rook blocks with Rf7, it's checkmate after Qxf7#. If Black captures with Qxf6, then e7+ wins material. The key lesson: a forcing check that limits the opponent's options and threatens mate often wins more decisively than immediately winning material.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qf6+\", \"line\": [\"Qf6+\", \"Rf7\", \"Qxf7#\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"attraction\", \"mate\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/3r3p/1p1pP1p1/1PpP4/2P2p2/4b3/1Q4PP/4R2K w - - 0 35"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/3r3p/1p1pP1p1/1PpP4/2P2p2/4b3/1Q4PP/4R2K w - - 0 35"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/3r3p/1p1pP1p1/1PpP4/2P2p2/4b3/1Q4PP/4R2K w - - 0 35", "move": "Rxe8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/3r3p/1p1pP1p1/1PpP4/2P2p2/4b3/1Q4PP/4R2K w - - 0 35", "move": "Qb8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/3r3p/1p1pP1p1/1PpP4/2P2p2/4b3/1Q4PP/4R2K w - - 0 35", "move": "Qf2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/3r3p/1p1pP1p1/1PpP4/2P2p2/4b3/1Q4PP/4R2K w - - 0 35", "move": "Qxd8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/3r3p/1p1pP1p1/1PpP4/2P2p2/4b3/1Q4PP/4R2K w - - 0 35", "move": "Re8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/3r3p/1p1pP1p1/1PpP4/2